experience.description:
- Assisted Muhammad Adeel Zaffar, Assistant Professor – Suleman Dawood School of Business;
- Assisted Mohammad Basharullah, Visiting Faculty – Suleman Dawood School of Business;
- Assisted Shezeen Salim Hemani, Teaching Fellow – Suleman Dawood School of Business.

- Received Top Intern Award, Unilever Internship Program (ULIP) 2015;
- Analyzed and cleaned the historic sales data of each of the company’s 448 active SKU’s for anomalies and non-repeatable events to derive the “pure” sales figures;
- Developed and built a dynamic baseline forecasting model to improve forecasting accuracy that is currently being used by the company’s demand planners.

- Led a team of environmental and civil engineers;
- Developed a system for assessing company, financial, health, safety, social and environmental risk;
- Designed and implemented the QHSE Management System for the operations phase of the project;
- Established the company’s Key Performance Indicators across all business functions; and
- Managed the environmental performance of the construction contractors.

- Project managed the delivery of pre-feasibility and feasibility studies into mine pit closure that were used in investment decisions requiring over $100m of capital spend at ERA – Ranger;
- Constructed net present value models to evaluate the viability of tailings management options for significant expansions that required capital investments of over $200m at ERA – Ranger and Northparkes Mine;
- Developed corporate responses to government papers relating to proposed emissions trading schemes, mandatory energy renewable targets and other related climate change and energy issues; and
- Created strategic environment plans for Rio Tinto operations in Australia and Argentina.
